@{
    Layout = "_LandingLayout";
    ViewData["Title"] = "Biosecurity Data Confidentiality & Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-5 my-4">
    <div class="card border-0 shadow-sm p-4 p-md-5" style="border-radius: var(--radius-md);">
        <h2 class="fw-bold text-success mb-3">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-shield-halved me-2"></i>Biosecurity Data Governance & Privacy Policy
        </h2>
        <p class="lead text-muted">
            FarmShield is committed to securing agricultural epidemiological records, proprietary breeding lineages, and biosecurity audit evaluations.
        </p>
        <hr class="my-4">

        <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2">1. Veterinary & Disease Surveillance Confidentiality</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            Reports of suspected or confirmed pathogen outbreaks (e.g., African Swine Fever, Avian Influenza) are classified under strict state-level agricultural data protection protocols. Access is restricted to authorized Farm Owners, verified Veterinary Officers, and State Animal Health Authorities.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2 mt-4">2. Farm Perimeter & Visitor Screening Records</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            Personal identity information collected at facility biosecurity checkpoints (including vehicle registration and 72-hour contact histories) is retained strictly for contact tracing and epidemiological containment in the event of an outbreak.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold text-dark mb-2 mt-4">3. Regulatory Compliance Standards</h5>
        <p class="text-secondary">
            Our data protection infrastructure complies with national livestock traceability standards and international animal health regulations established by WOAH (World Organisation for Animal Health).
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
